 "descripcion": "Hou Yi shot down nine suns and left one. As a reward, he was given the elixir of immortality, but only enough for one.\n\nSources: Huainanzi, chapters 6 and 8.\n\nWould you drink it?\n\n#mythology #chinesemythology #change #houyi #shorts",
 "lineas": [
  {
   "texto": "Hou Yi shot nine suns. Each one fell as a golden crow.",
   "pausa": 0.6
  },
  {
   "texto": "He left one, so the world would still have light.",
   "pausa": 0.6
  },
  {
   "texto": "He became a hero, and he married Chang'e.",
   "pausa": 0.6
  },
  {
   "texto": "The Queen Mother of the West gave him a gift.",
   "pausa": 0.6
  },
  {
   "texto": "The elixir of immortality. Live forever.",
   "pausa": 0.6
  },
  {
   "texto": "But only enough for one person.",
   "pausa": 0.6
  },
  {
   "texto": "He didn't want forever without her, so he hid it.",
   "pausa": 0.6
  },
  {
   "texto": "And one day, someone found it. Part three, {when_next}.",
   "pausa": 0.3
  }
 ],
